  "_id": "6a7f5797757ee51246381afc",
  "lab": "6a7f5796eda1a5feaff0b458",
  "name": "LIVER FUNCTION TEST (LFT)",
  "code": "LFT",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>\n<div>Test</div>\n</th>\n<th>\n<div>Interpretation</div>\n</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<div>Total protein</div>\n</td>\n<td>\n<div>Total protein measures the total amount of protein in the blood, including albumin and globulin. Abnormal results may indicate liver or kidney disease, malnutrition, or inflammation.</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<div>Albumin</div>\n</td>\n<td>\n<div>Albumin is a protein produced by the liver. Abnormal results may indicate liver or kidney disease, malnutrition, or inflammation.</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<div>Bilirubin</div>\n</td>\n<td>\n<div>Bilirubin is a substance produced by the breakdown of red blood cells. Abnormal results may indicate liver disease or other conditions affecting the liver or gallbladder.</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<div>Alkaline phosphatase (ALP)</div>\n</td>\n<td>\n<div>ALP is an enzyme produced by the liver and other organs. Abnormal results may indicate liver or bone disease, or certain medications.</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<div>Alanine transaminase (ALT)/ SGPT</div>\n</td>\n<td>\n<div>ALT is an enzyme primarily produced by the liver. Abnormal results may indicate liver damage or disease.</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<div>Aspartate transaminase (AST)/ SGOT</div>\n</td>\n<td>\n<div>AST is an enzyme produced by the liver and other organs. Abnormal results may indicate liver damage or disease.</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
